changes.change:
(a) `(plan-stats db entries)`, with entries `[[path size mtime-ms] ...]`, returns `[[path reason] ...]` only for entries needing a read:
- `:new` when there is no eid;
- `:no-stat` when `(attr-v db eid :file/size)` is nil;
- `:stat-changed` when `(not (same-stat? size' (attr-v db eid :file/last-modified-at) size mtime-ms))`.

(b) Extend compare-contents to take `[[path content trusted-size mtime-ms] ...]`. For content-equal entries with a non-nil trusted-size whose stored stat differs, collect `{:db/id eid :file/size s :file/last-modified-at (js/Date. mtime-ms)}` and apply one `ldb/transact!` per call with tx-meta `{:reconcile/stats? true}`. Compare and transact run in one synchronous worker task, so the content cannot change in between and the invariant holds. For file-only datoms the per-tx search sync filters to nothing (search.cljs:776-779) but still commits one watermark (search_indexer.cljs:548-553): one small commit per 32-file call.

When `(not db-graph?)`, also remove `:file/size` and `:file/last-modified-at` datoms (optionally `:file/created-at`, 10 058 datoms today). Otherwise the backfill adds about 20k datoms to the 93k boot reply and to the UI conn build. UI readers checked:
- native_fs.cljs:171-189 uses select-keys incl. last-modified-at, but `modified` is computed from content only (185-189);
- components/file.cljs:35-47 reads through the worker (`<get-files` with `:transact-db? false`, db/async.cljs:30-37);
- db/async.cljs:37 falls back to 0.

Visible change: the All-files table will show real mtimes after backfill.

Worker, on an in-memory conn:
- compare-contents: equal, changed, whitespace-only change, missing entity;
- plan-stats: equal stat, size nil, mtime differs, size differs;
- stat recording: trusted is written; racy, or content differs, is not.

Invariant:
- set-file-content! and set-file-last-modified-at! retract :file/size for a new and for an existing path, through the outliner :transact op;
- parse-file without :size on an existing file retracts it; with :size it sets both;
- the listener guard reports zero violations across the graph-parser suite.

Differential: over a fixture graph plus a disk-mutation matrix (unchanged, content changed with a different size, same size with a new mtime, new file, blank new file, deleted, hidden path, custom.css), the set of paths handed to handle-changed! must be a superset of what the old loop acted on. The only permitted exception, in Step 3, is the forged case: same size and mtime reset to the stored value.
